{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Charts releases before 1.0 follow this Alpha policy. Packages use regular "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.x"},{"type":"text","value":" versions on the normal\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"latest"},{"type":"text","value":" npm tag, without an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-alpha"},{"type":"text","value":" suffix or separate release channel."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alpha is ready for evaluation and early application integration. It is not a\nstable API promise. Pin an exact version in production applications and test an\nupgrade before changing that pin."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"version-contract","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Version contract"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All public TanStack Charts packages move together as one fixed release group."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Patch releases fix defects and do not intentionally remove or rename public\nAPIs. A fix may correct rendering or interaction that was observably wrong."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Minor releases may add features and may contain breaking API changes while\nthe package major remains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"./compatibility.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stable compatibility contract"}]},{"type":"text","value":" takes effect with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1.0"},{"type":"text","value":"; published "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.x"},{"type":"text","value":" releases continue to follow this Alpha policy."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"public-surface","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Public surface"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The public surface is the package export map and the APIs documented on this\nsite. Source files, internal modules, unexported types, generated scene details,\nand undocumented behavior may change without a migration path."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework adapters share the same chart definition and release version. Their\nruntime support and peer ranges are listed in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./installation.md#framework-compatibility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"breaking-changes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Breaking changes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A breaking Alpha release must include a changeset, changelog entry, and concrete\nmigration instructions. We will use a development warning ahead of removal when\nthat warning is practical and useful, but Alpha does not promise a minimum\ndeprecation window."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production bundles do not retain development migration warnings. Removed APIs\nfail through TypeScript or an actionable runtime error instead of silently\nfalling back to an older interpretation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"report-a-regression","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Report a regression"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/charts/issues/new/choose","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open a GitHub issue"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with\nthe exact package version, framework, browser or native runtime, a minimal\nreproduction, and the expected and actual result. A regression in a patch\nrelease is treated as a defect against this policy."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"version-contract","text":"Version contract","level":2},{"id":"public-surface","text":"Public surface","level":2},{"id":"breaking-changes","text":"Breaking changes","level":2},{"id":"report-a-regression","text":"Report a regression","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Charts releases before 1.0 follow this Alpha policy. Packages use regular `0.x` versions on the normal\n`latest` npm tag, without an `-alpha` suffix or separate release channel.\n\nAlpha is ready for evaluation and early application integration. It is not a\nstable API promise. Pin an exact version in production applications and test an\nupgrade before changing that pin.\n\n## Version contract\n\nAll public TanStack Charts packages move together as one fixed release group.\n\n- Patch releases fix defects and do not intentionally remove or rename public\n  APIs. A fix may correct rendering or interaction that was observably wrong.\n- Minor releases may add features and may contain breaking API changes while\n  the package major remains `0`.\n- The [stable compatibility contract](./compatibility.md) takes effect with\n  `1.0`; published `0.x` releases continue to follow this Alpha policy.\n\n## Public surface\n\nThe public surface is the package export map and the APIs documented on this\nsite. Source files, internal modules, unexported types, generated scene details,\nand undocumented behavior may change without a migration path.\n\nFramework adapters share the same chart definition and release version. Their\nruntime support and peer ranges are listed in\n[Installation](./installation.md#framework-compatibility).\n\n## Breaking changes\n\nA breaking Alpha release must include a changeset, changelog entry, and concrete\nmigration instructions. We will use a development warning ahead of removal when\nthat warning is practical and useful, but Alpha does not promise a minimum\ndeprecation window.\n\nProduction bundles do not retain development migration warnings. Removed APIs\nfail through TypeScript or an actionable runtime error instead of silently\nfalling back to an older interpretation.\n\n## Report a regression\n\n[Open a GitHub issue](https://github.com/TanStack/charts/issues/new/choose) with\nthe exact package version, framework, browser or native runtime, a minimal\nreproduction, and the expected and actual result. A regression in a patch\nrelease is treated as a defect against this policy.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Alpha Stability\ndescription: Understand what TanStack Charts Alpha versions promise, what may change, and how releases communicate breaking changes.\n---\n\nTanStack Charts releases before 1.0 follow this Alpha policy. Packages use regular `0.x` versions on the normal\n`latest` npm tag, without an `-alpha` suffix or separate release channel.\n\nAlpha is ready for evaluation and early application integration. It is not a\nstable API promise. Pin an exact version in production applications and test an\nupgrade before changing that pin.\n\n## Version contract\n\nAll public TanStack Charts packages move together as one fixed release group.\n\n- Patch releases fix defects and do not intentionally remove or rename public\n  APIs. A fix may correct rendering or interaction that was observably wrong.\n- Minor releases may add features and may contain breaking API changes while\n  the package major remains `0`.\n- The [stable compatibility contract](./compatibility.md) takes effect with\n  `1.0`; published `0.x` releases continue to follow this Alpha policy.\n\n## Public surface\n\nThe public surface is the package export map and the APIs documented on this\nsite. Source files, internal modules, unexported types, generated scene details,\nand undocumented behavior may change without a migration path.\n\nFramework adapters share the same chart definition and release version. Their\nruntime support and peer ranges are listed in\n[Installation](./installation.md#framework-compatibility).\n\n## Breaking changes\n\nA breaking Alpha release must include a changeset, changelog entry, and concrete\nmigration instructions. We will use a development warning ahead of removal when\nthat warning is practical and useful, but Alpha does not promise a minimum\ndeprecation window.\n\nProduction bundles do not retain development migration warnings. Removed APIs\nfail through TypeScript or an actionable runtime error instead of silently\nfalling back to an older interpretation.\n\n## Report a regression\n\n[Open a GitHub issue](https://github.com/TanStack/charts/issues/new/choose) with\nthe exact package version, framework, browser or native runtime, a minimal\nreproduction, and the expected and actual result. A regression in a patch\nrelease is treated as a defect against this policy.\n"}
